        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "9db22399-458f-5dd5-a685-ba31db4c65d3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Portland International Airport, Gerald R. Ford International Airport, Cascade Township, Grand Rapids, Michigan, Oregon\n- Organizations: 454th Bombardment Group, 454th Troop Carrier Wing, Continental Air Command\n- Concepts: Airport identifiers, civil-military airports, commercial airports\n\nFacts:\n- Portland International Airport has the identifiers IATA PDX, ICAO KPDX, and FAA LID PDX.\n- Portland International Airport is a joint civil-military airport in Oregon and is the largest airport in the state.\n- Portland International Airport accounts for 90 percent of Oregon passenger travel and more than 95 percent of the state's air cargo.\n- Gerald R. Ford International Airport has the identifiers IATA GRR, ICAO KGRR, and FAA LID GRR.\n- Gerald R. Ford International Airport is a commercial airport in Cascade Township about 13 miles southeast of Grand Rapids, Michigan.\n- The 454th Bombardment Group was last assigned to the 454th Troop Carrier Wing of Continental Air Command at Portland International Airport in Oregon.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
